+## Run examples
 
-## 📦 Build Instructions
+```bash
+cd build
+./wblsSim run_Cs137.mac
+./wblsSim run_Na22.mac
+./wblsSim run_Co60.mac
+```
+
+The macros are copied into the build directory by CMake.  Geometry/material UI
+commands must be set before `/run/initialize`.
+
+## ROOT output
+
+The output file name is controlled with:
+
+```text
+/wbls/output/file Cs137_wbls.root
+```
+
+Two TTrees are written:
+
+### `events`
+
+- `eventID`
+- `sourceType`
+- `nPrimaryGammas`
+- `primaryEnergySum_keV`
+- `edepWbLS_keV`
+- `nOpticalProducedWbLS`
+- `nCerenkovProducedWbLS`
+- `nScintProducedWbLS`
+- `nDetectedLargePMT`, `nDetectedSmallPMT`
+- `nDetectedLargePMT_Cerenkov`, `nDetectedSmallPMT_Cerenkov`
+- `nDetectedLargePMT_Scintillation`, `nDetectedSmallPMT_Scintillation`
+
+### `photons`
+
+One row per detected optical photon when `/wbls/output/savePhotonTree true`:
+
+- `eventID`
+- `pmtID` (`0=largePMT`, `1=smallPMT`)
+- `wavelength_nm`
+- `detectionTime_ns`
+- `creationProcess` (`Scintillation`, `Cerenkov`, or `unknown`)
+- `parentTrackID`
+- `creatorProcessName`
+- `originX_mm`, `originY_mm`, `originZ_mm`
+- `hitX_mm`, `hitY_mm`, `hitZ_mm`
+
+## Preserving scintillation vs Cherenkov information
+
+`G4SteppingAction` inspects optical secondaries produced during steps in the
+WbLS logical volume.  Each optical photon receives a small `PhotonTrackInfo`
+object that stores its creator process name, origin position, and parent track
+ID.  When that photon reaches either PMT, the tag is used to increment separate
+Cherenkov and scintillation counters and to fill the per-photon TTree.
+
+## Runtime knobs and edit points
+
+Common macro commands:
+
+```text
+/wbls/sphere/radius 10 cm
+/wbls/ports/sampleDiameter 3 cm
+/wbls/ports/largePMTDiameter 5 cm
+/wbls/ports/smallPMTDiameter 2.5 cm
+/wbls/cuvette/radius 1 cm
+/wbls/cuvette/height 4 cm
+/wbls/cuvette/wall 1 mm
+/wbls/cuvette/insertion 1 cm
+/wbls/source/isotope Cs137
+/wbls/source/radius 4 mm
+/wbls/source/thickness 1 mm
+/wbls/source/distance 2 mm
+/wbls/wbls/lightYield 9000 1/MeV
+/wbls/wbls/absScale 1.0
+/wbls/spectralon/reflectivity 0.98
+/wbls/pmt/largeQEScale 1.0
+/wbls/pmt/smallQEScale 1.0
+```
+
+For wavelength-dependent replacements, edit the clearly marked arrays in
+`G4DetectorConstruction.cc`:
+
+- WbLS refractive index, absorption length, Rayleigh length, scintillation
+  spectrum, yield, decay time, and Birks constant.
+- Quartz refractive index and UV absorption cutoff.
+- Spectralon reflectivity curve.
+- Large/small PMT QE curves.
+
+## Validation plots
+
+After producing a ROOT file:
 
 ```bash
-mkdir build && cd build
-cmake ..
-make
-./g4Sim
+python3 scripts/plot_wbls.py build/Cs137_wbls.root --outdir plots
+```
+
+The script writes plots for WbLS energy deposition, detected PE distributions,
+largePMT-vs-smallPMT counts, scintillation-vs-Cherenkov detected totals,
+detected-photon wavelength spectra, and detection-time spectra.
+
+## Intentional simplifications
+
+- The sphere ports are represented by the top cuvette opening and by ideal PMT
+  disks placed just inside the spherical wall; no detailed mechanical port cuts
+  or PMT glass bulbs are modeled.
+- The source encapsulation is represented only by an inactive disk placement and
+  an isotropic gamma starting distribution.
+- The WbLS, quartz, Spectralon, and QE curves are plausible placeholders for
+  toy studies, not tuned measurements.
